From e62076d202bf9ad1d8ddceb09e0ad1a1eccb4e99 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 17:31:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix AI dish-scan race condition and multi-item loss; harden
 server validation
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- docs/js/ai.js, docs/js/app.js: an in-flight AI request (photo or text
  submit) is no longer left to race a second one — double-tapping "تحليل",
  pressing Enter while a request is pending, or picking a new photo mid-
  analysis used to fire overlapping API calls with whichever response
  resolved last silently overwriting the other (discarding it and its
  cost with zero trace). Now the previous request is aborted via
  AbortController (plus a sequence-number backstop) and the trigger
  controls (analyze/camera/gallery/text input) are disabled while a
  request is in flight.
- docs/js/ai.js, docs/js/app.js: fixed a high-severity UX bug where
  tapping one item from a multi-item AI scan (to review/save it in the
  manual-entry form) silently destroyed the rest of that scan's results —
  reopening the AI sheet always did a full reset, forcing a complete
  re-scan (another paid API call) to deal with item 2 of a 3-item plate.
  Unhandled items are now preserved and restored on next open.
- docs/js/ai.js: exact-string library-name matching against the AI's
  reply is fragile for Arabic text (stray diacritics/whitespace/NFC vs
  NFKC); added a normalized-comparison fallback so a near-miss doesn't
  wrongly fall through to "no match found" when the food actually exists.
- docs/js/ai.js: a raw English "Failed to fetch" from a real network
  failure was leaking into an otherwise fully-Arabic UI; now shown as a
  proper Arabic message.
- docs/index.html, docs/js/app.js: the library/general mode toggle was
  keyboard-inoperable (plain divs, click-only) — added role="button",
  tabindex, aria-pressed, and Enter/Space handling; added min="0" to the
  manual macro-entry fields.
- docs/css/styles.css: added :disabled styling for .btn-secondary and the
  AI sheet's text input, needed for the new in-flight-disable behavior.
- server/ai-proxy-worker.js: clamped AI-derived macro numbers to a
  generous sane range (previously unbounded — a hallucinated/malformed
  reply could write a negative or absurd number straight into the food
  library with no check anywhere in the pipeline); bumped
  max_output_tokens from 800 to 2048 since a full multi-item reply (up to
  12 items, several numeric fields + name each) risked truncation right
  on the photos this feature is meant to handle best.

Investigated via one code-review pass and one live Playwright scenario
suite (12 scenarios incl. double-submit, HTTP errors, malformed JSON,
offline) against the AI dish-scan flow; findings verified before fixing,
and the full existing regression suite (undo, weight card, streak,
template delete, water bidi, select resets, AI text/general mode) re-run
clean afterward.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
